\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>These landmarks, along with the breathtaking views of the valley and its natural beauty, make Sublime Point a popular tourist destination and a must-visit for those exploring the Blue Mountains.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Yes, Narrow Neck Plateau is considered a mesa. A mesa is a flat-topped, elevated landform with steep cliffs or sides. Narrow Neck Plateau is a narrow strip of sandstone plateau that runs between the Jamison Valley and the Megalong Valley in the Blue Mountains of New South Wales, Australia. The plateau was formed through millions of years of erosion and uplift, leaving behind a flat-topped landform that rises dramatically above the surrounding valleys. The steep cliffs of the plateau are a result of the differential weathering and erosion of the sandstone, which is more resistant in some areas than others. As a result, Narrow Neck Plateau qualifies as a mesa.
